<Base title="About" description="About Adam Bloebaum.">
  <div class="index-head"><h1 class="page-title">About</h1></div>
  <div class="about">
    <div class="prose">
      <p>I work as an Applied Quantitative Engineer at Driveline Baseball, developing predictive biomechanics models, creating computer vision tools, building robust data pipelines, and crafting products that help push player development forward.</p>
      <p>I'm also a minor league pitcher for the Washington Nationals, giving me a unique perspective as both a builder and a user of the tools I create.</p>
      <p>I completed my undergraduate work in physics and data science at the University of Washington, specializing in biophysics. While there, I developed a strong math and science foundation and found interest in machine learning.</p>
      <p>I'm currently pursuing my Master of Science in Analytics at Georgia Tech, focusing on advanced modeling and high-performance computing.</p>
      <p>Find me on <a href="https://x.com/bl0ebaum">X</a>, <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/adambloebaum/">LinkedIn</a>, and <a href="https://github.com/adambloebaum">GitHub</a>.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="photos">
      <img src="/images/about-me.jpg" alt="Adam Bloebaum at work at Driveline Baseball" />
      <img src="/images/about-me2.jpg" alt="Adam Bloebaum pitching for the Fredericksburg Nationals" />
    </div>
  </div>
